duction release that was healthy is v2.3.0. v2.3.1 is the unhealthy one currently running in all three regions. I'll roll back to v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01UrPAruzvuYd4eUrjt1gSrk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018aSGg3G3dVFrUmfFRJAAQT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01E35dZaiPaJYGbaFHUXHkav", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after v2.3.1 was deployed to production (us-east, us-west, eu-west); error rate was about 0.18. Action taken: rolled back checkout-api to v2.3.0 in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). v2.3.0 is the most recent production release that was healthy (v2.3.1 was unhealthy and v2.3.1-rc was unhealthy in staging). The rollback reported VERIFIED. Follow-up: confirm the health and error rate after rollback and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back from v2.3.1 to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and the service is healthy again.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** It is the most recent production release marked healthy. v2.3.1 is the unhealthy release that was running, and v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy (staging only).\n- **Post-rollback status:** healthy, error rate down from about 0.18 to 0.002.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident **INC-0001** for checkout-api. It describes the failure, the rollback, and the reason for choosing v2.3.0. It also paged the on-call engineer.\n\nThe rollback did not need change-manager approval because v2.3.0 was previously healthy in production. Before v2.3.1 is redeployed, someone needs to find out why it failed health checks.", "type": "text"}]}]}